# Shell scripts run on Linux, and dietpi/install.sh is fetched straight from
# raw.githubusercontent.com and piped into sh. If a Windows checkout ever
# committed it back with CRLF endings, that one-liner would fail for everyone
# with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" - and it would be invisible on the machine
# that caused it, because there it still works.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same hazard, no extension to match on: this one is a shell script fetched and
# run on Linux, and is also installed to /usr/local/bin as the peekesp command.
dietpi/peekesp text eol=lf

# Firmware images and icons must never be line-ending "corrected".
*.bin binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
